# Architecture

## Layer Structure

```
app/              → Presentation (React components, pages, hooks)
application/      → Use cases (orchestration, DTOs)
core/             → Domain logic (types, business rules)
infrastructure/   → Data access (DB, external APIs)
```

## Dependency Rules

| Layer | Can Import From | Cannot Import From |
|-------|----------------|-------------------|
| `app/` | `application/` only | `core/`, `infrastructure/` |
| `application/` | `core/` only | `infrastructure/` |
| `core/` | Nothing | Any other layer |
| `infrastructure/` | `core/` only | `application/`, `app/` |

**Why?** Changes in one layer don't cascade. Each layer can be tested in isolation.

## Data Flow

```
User Action → app/ (calls) → application/ (uses) → core/ (calls) → infrastructure/ → DB
                                                    ↓
                                            ResponseWrapper<DTO>
```

See `07-implementation-patterns.mdc` for implementation patterns.

## DTOs (Data Transfer Objects)

- All data sent to client **must be DTOs** (fully serializable)
- DTOs live in `application/dto-types/`
- Always serialize `Date` → `string` (ISO 8601)

```typescript
export type UserDTO = Omit<User, 'password'> & {
  createdAt: string
}
```

## Rules

- Never bypass layers (e.g., `app/` → `infrastructure/`)
- Never import domain types in presentation layer
- Never create circular dependencies
